<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 30-MAY.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 30-MAY.</headline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Marie, with 80 mph winds, is in the open waters of the western Pacific near 20n/160e, moving north at 9 mph. This system will continue to strengthen during the next 24 hours before beginning to weaken. It tracks over the open waters of the western Pacific and thus is only a significant threat to shipping.  </p>
<p>There are no other statements at this time.</p>
</text>
